  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Core System**\n\nI\'m focusing on defining the core system, ELMANEKO 3D 2.0. We are tasked to build a full-featured management system for 3D printing. Initially, the project scope includes simulated authentication with full capabilities, so we have a solid foundation for user access and security. I\'m exploring the system architecture to support features like print job management.\n\n\n**Considering Client-Side Design**\n\nI\'m now seriously considering building a robust client-side SPA using standard React since Supabase isn\'t listed as a provisionable platform, and we don\'t have specified dependencies on any third-party APIs beyond the potential for Gemini in the future. I\'m prioritizing offline functionality and responsiveness in the client-side database layer. This seems to be the best and safest approach.\n\n\n**Embracing Client-Side Architecture**\n\nI\'ve decided to fully embrace a client-side approach. My current focus is on a high-fidelity React SPA, built with Tailwind CSS. This system will simulate backend operations, managing client data, filaments, purchases, printers, and energy tariffs entirely on the client-side. The goal is a seamless user experience that behaves like a backend would.\n\n\n**Expanding System Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the system\'s scope to include Printed Products with Bill of Materials, a Production module for order management and cost calculation, and Budgets with automatic totals and conversion to sales.\n\nI\'m also working on Sales, a comprehensive Dashboard with indicators and charts, and a PDF Generator for invoices. Backup & Restore functionality, including a full export and selective restore, is crucial. Additionally, an SQL Script generator for Supabase is being considered for advanced users.\n\n\n**Analyzing Project Requirements**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the initial project files and requirements more closely, specifically to confirm the need for Firebase or Cloud SQL and ensure I haven\'t missed any crucial dependencies. The client did mention the usage of Tailwind CSS and Shadcn UI, so I\'m considering the potential integration of Shadcn UI as I build customizable Tailwind components. I\'m also ensuring that these elements of the project are the cleanest and most high-end as possible.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Aesthetic Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual and functional aspects. I want a sharp, responsive, and fully typed UI, so I\'m aiming for a contrast-rich orange/black/white theme, avoiding complex CLI installations that might fail. I\'m prioritizing gorgeous custom components that meet these high standards. I also need to generate a beautiful logo for ELMANEKO 3D, and will decide whether to leverage the image-generation skill or create an exquisite CSS/SVG-based logo for robustness.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now check the contents of `metadata.json` and `package.json` to understand the structure of the application and its dependencies, ensuring that we name the app properly and install any packages if necessary (e.g., `recharts` for dashboards)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 114127287
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
