  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Project Authentication**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the authentication module for ELMANEKO 3D 2.0. This includes the login page (email/password), forgot password, and logout functionalities. I\'m aiming for a robust implementation using simulated client-side storage to mimic Supabase Auth\'s behavior effectively, ensuring a smooth user experience.\n\n\n**Outlining Filament Inventory**\n\nI\'m now outlining \"M\303\223DULO 2,\" focusing on filament inventory: PLA, PETG, ABS, and TPU. I\'m detailing the fields: ID, name, type, brand, color, total/available weight, purchase value, date, supplier, and notes. The key formula will be value per gram. I\'m also planning a sidebar summary with stock totals, value, type breakdowns, and low-stock alerts.\n\n\n**Calculating Project Costs**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to cost calculations within ELMANEKO. I\'m nailing down formulas for filament costs, using the maximum value per gram across same filament types. Energy costs are calculated, and labor costs are specified per unit. I\'ve also incorporated markup percentages for profit margin, finalizing the final price calculation, and then the implementation! I\'m planning out the necessary tables and fields to contain all cost data.\n\n\n**Defining Production Flows**\n\nI\'m now outlining production run operations, focusing on the consumption of raw filaments and the creation of finished products which will populate a product inventory. Sales actions deduct from finished product inventories, whether sales come directly or are created via a budget. I am now focused on defining what information is necessary for a production run.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now install the `recharts` package to enable high-quality dashboards and charts for tracking sales, production, energy consumption, and stock levels."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 324152712
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
